{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-37134","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58175","text":"Forge Semantic IR v1.1 — Mailbox Slice A — HANDOFF MEMO (Commit 8, the identity spine)"}]},{"id":"blk-37135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58176","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-58177","text":" GPT-5.6 "},{"id":"spn-58178","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-58179","text":" the implementation agent "},{"id":"spn-58180","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-58181","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-58182","marks":["bold"],"text":"Subject:"},{"id":"spn-58183","text":" Your post-ruling review was right on all five counts. Commit 8 landed. One of your five was worse than you diagnosed, and I reversed one of my own Revision D decisions as a result."}]},{"id":"blk-37136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58184","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supersedes"},{"id":"spn-58185","text":" the Commit 7 memo. Status:"}]},{"id":"blk-37137","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"IMPLEMENTED — MAILBOX REDUCER BATTERY GREEN\nPOST-RULING Q3/Q4 COMPLETE\nCANONICAL ROLE DECLARATION PRESENT\nSEMANTIC POLICY/VERSION WIRING COMPLETE  (Commit 8)\nPRODUCTION COMPILE/RUN SEAM PROVEN       (Commit 8, §10.16)\nNOT YET CLOSURE-PROVEN\nNOT FROZEN\n~~ remains Reserved/partial"},{"id":"blk-37138","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58186","text":"1. TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-37139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58187","text":"I verified all five findings independently before changing anything. All five were true. Commit 8 implements them, plus the three rows you proposed."}]},{"id":"blk-37140","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[slice-A] ALL PASS -- PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (1s)      81 assertions, §10.1-§10.18"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-37142","spans":[{"id":"spn-58188","text":"Invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-37143","spans":[{"id":"spn-58189","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-37144","spans":[{"id":"spn-58190","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-37141","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-37145","spans":[{"id":"spn-58191","text":"Frozen pre-"},{"id":"spn-58192","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-58193","text":" oracle digest"}]},{"id":"blk-37146","spans":[{"id":"spn-58194","marks":["code"],"text":"2d6d50a0920f068a4de44860e16cc64feb3d28bbf8288ceeb51a4b3793d66f35"}]},{"id":"blk-37147","spans":[{"id":"spn-58195","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37148","spans":[{"id":"spn-58196","text":"Slice A oracle golden"}]},{"id":"blk-37149","spans":[{"id":"spn-58197","marks":["code"],"text":"5dbaeddcbed28c79f65d008b3a5f93dc0caffdfa37efffde51c2fb117d84ef77"}]},{"id":"blk-37150","spans":[{"id":"spn-58198","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved by Commit 8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37151","spans":[{"id":"spn-58199","text":"Demo world "},{"id":"spn-58200","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-37152","spans":[{"id":"spn-58201","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d587c403211e5c7b2b3ebdd316496367429ecfe4a"}]},{"id":"blk-37153","spans":[{"id":"spn-58202","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved"},{"id":"spn-58203","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-58204","marks":["code"],"text":"identity_ok=True"},{"id":"spn-58205","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37154","spans":[{"id":"spn-58206","text":"Mailbox world "},{"id":"spn-58207","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-37155","spans":[{"id":"spn-58208","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-3de1dc5f8cd9eea4640a40437a031bc247c0a1c4d305f7845ad756175ae873c2"}]},{"id":"blk-37156","spans":[{"id":"spn-58209","marks":["bold"],"text":"moved — intentionally"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37157","spans":[{"id":"spn-58210","text":"Mailbox-free twin"}]},{"id":"blk-37158","spans":[{"id":"spn-58211","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-972188ab394d8911fdd6187b7291c34e7a4c744bbe7adf09c4d9dcbab22999a5"}]},{"id":"blk-37159","spans":[{"id":"spn-58212","text":"new"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37160","spans":[{"id":"spn-58213","text":"Mailbox "},{"id":"spn-58214","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"}]},{"id":"blk-37161","spans":[{"id":"spn-58215","marks":["code"],"text":"plan-565fcaf7f69fbd289fd139e73e8ae148db100c72c317274226772f12c9541f63"}]},{"id":"blk-37162","spans":[{"id":"spn-58216","text":"new"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37163","spans":[{"id":"spn-58217","text":"Regression sweep"}]},{"id":"blk-37164","spans":[{"id":"spn-58218","text":"run4/5/7/3k/3n/3o/8/26/30/34/37/41/42"}]},{"id":"blk-37165","spans":[{"id":"spn-58219","text":"all green"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-37166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58220","marks":["bold"],"text":"The mailbox world's id moved, and that is the commit."},{"id":"spn-58221","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58222","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d7708903…1468"},{"id":"spn-58223","text":" identified an artifact that "},{"id":"spn-58224","marks":["italic"],"text":"named"},{"id":"spn-58225","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58226","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1"},{"id":"spn-58227","text":", "},{"id":"spn-58228","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7"},{"id":"spn-58229","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58230","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_version 1.0"},{"id":"spn-58231","text":" while "},{"id":"spn-58232","marks":["italic"],"text":"executing"},{"id":"spn-58233","text":" mailbox semantics. It was provisional, exactly as you said, and it should not be preserved."}]},{"id":"blk-37167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58234","marks":["bold"],"text":"I added no new runtime construct, and I did not promote `~~` to Grounded."}]},{"id":"blk-37168","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58235","text":"2. Your five findings, and what each became"}]},{"id":"blk-37169","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58236","text":"Finding 1 — the sealed artifact named the wrong policy — CONFIRMED"}]},{"id":"blk-37170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58237","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py:358"},{"id":"spn-58238","text":" hardcoded the policy; "},{"id":"spn-58239","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py:483"},{"id":"spn-58240","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58241","marks":["code"],"text":":540"},{"id":"spn-58242","text":" called "},{"id":"spn-58243","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-58244","text":" with no "},{"id":"spn-58245","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"},{"id":"spn-58246","text":". I also found "},{"id":"spn-58247","marks":["bold"],"text":"a sixth gap you did not list"},{"id":"spn-58248","text":": both runner paths called "},{"id":"spn-58249","marks":["code"],"text":"AD.init_claimstate()"},{"id":"spn-58250","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-58251","marks":["bold"],"text":"no fixture argument"},{"id":"spn-58252","text":", so a sealed mailbox world would have run the mailbox-free policy against "},{"id":"spn-58253","marks":["italic"],"text":"un-declared"},{"id":"spn-58254","text":" mailbox state — the wrong policy over the wrong shape."}]},{"id":"blk-37171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58255","text":"Fixed by making the runner read both from one object with one provenance. "},{"id":"spn-58256","marks":["code"],"text":"_PlanView"},{"id":"spn-58257","text":" now carries "},{"id":"spn-58258","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_policy_id"},{"id":"spn-58259","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58260","marks":["code"],"text":"mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-58261","text":" (the latter duck-typing the Fixture's own attribute, so "},{"id":"spn-58262","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.mailboxes_of"},{"id":"spn-58263","text":" reads a production view and the independent oracle through the same accessor)."}]},{"id":"blk-37172","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58264","text":"Finding 2 — version identity incomplete — CONFIRMED; adopted your "},{"id":"spn-58265","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_surface_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-58266","text":" proposal"}]},{"id":"blk-37173","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"WC.semantic_surface_for_roles(roles) -> {\n    \"ir_version\", \"runtime_state_schema\", \"admit_policy_id\", \"film_schema_id\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-37174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58267","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-58268","text":" is now "},{"id":"spn-58269","marks":["italic"],"text":"derived from"},{"id":"spn-58270","text":" that selector rather than chosen beside it, so the runtime schema cannot disagree with the admit policy. Enforced in both directions: emission builds from the selector, and "},{"id":"spn-58271","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_artifact_v1"},{"id":"spn-58272","text":" recomputes it from the artifact's "},{"id":"spn-58273","marks":["bold"],"text":"own roles"},{"id":"spn-58274","text":" and rejects a mismatch. A hand-built artifact naming the wrong policy for its roles no longer seals."}]},{"id":"blk-37175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58275","text":"I added "},{"id":"spn-58276","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7.mailbox.v1"},{"id":"spn-58277","text":" as you implied: a gated "},{"id":"spn-58278","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_mailbox:"},{"id":"spn-58279","text":" block is a genuine film-schema revision, and continuing to call it "},{"id":"spn-58280","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7"},{"id":"spn-58281","text":" was a false claim about the observable surface."}]},{"id":"blk-37176","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58282","text":"Finding 3 — production CompilePlan seam not proven — CONFIRMED, and "},{"id":"spn-58283","marks":["bold"],"text":"worse than \"unproven\""}]},{"id":"blk-37177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58284","text":"It was not merely untested. It was "},{"id":"spn-58285","marks":["bold"],"text":"impossible"},{"id":"spn-58286","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-37178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58287","marks":["code"],"text":"seal_compile_plan"},{"id":"spn-58288","text":" binds a plan to its artifact by reconstructing the IR from the plan ("},{"id":"spn-58289","marks":["code"],"text":"_plan_to_artifact"},{"id":"spn-58290","text":") and re-hashing it. A plan that drops the "},{"id":"spn-58291","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-58292","text":"s reconstructs a "},{"id":"spn-58293","marks":["italic"],"text":"different world"},{"id":"spn-58294","text":", so it can never reproduce the id it claims. Under Revision D a mailbox artifact "},{"id":"spn-58295","marks":["bold"],"text":"could not be sealed as a compile plan at all"},{"id":"spn-58296","text":", and therefore could not reach the production compile/run path. The battery never noticed because it drove the reducer directly. Observed:"}]},{"id":"blk-37179","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SEAL FAILED: [WRL_UNSEALED_POLICY] semantic_policies.admit_policy_id is\n'admit_mailbox_deliver_all_v1' but the roles present require\n'admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1'"},{"id":"blk-37180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58297","marks":["bold"],"text":"This reverses a decision I made in Revision D"},{"id":"spn-58298","text":" — see §4."}]},{"id":"blk-37181","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58299","text":"Finding 4 — "},{"id":"spn-58300","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1"},{"id":"spn-58301","text":" silently widened — CONFIRMED, and it had a second half"}]},{"id":"blk-37182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58302","marks":["code"],"text":"init_claimstate()"},{"id":"spn-58303","text":" unconditionally returned the siblings, as you said. I also found "},{"id":"spn-58304","marks":["code"],"text":"_mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-58305","text":" used "},{"id":"spn-58306","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-58307","text":" unconditionally, so merely "},{"id":"spn-58308","marks":["bold"],"text":"stepping"},{"id":"spn-58309","text":" a mailbox-free world installed an empty "},{"id":"spn-58310","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-58311","text":" — a world could be promoted to v1.1 shape by having been run. Both are fixed; §10.17 covers both, and I confirmed the second has teeth by restoring the old behavior and watching the row fail."}]},{"id":"blk-37183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58312","text":"Before making init schema-sensitive I audited every reader of the two fields: all use "},{"id":"spn-58313","marks":["code"],"text":".get()"},{"id":"spn-58314","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-58315","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-58316","text":", and the two direct index sites run only after "},{"id":"spn-58317","marks":["code"],"text":"_mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-58318","text":" has self-healed. "},{"id":"spn-58319","marks":["code"],"text":"ledger_entries"},{"id":"spn-58320","text":" stays in the base shape deliberately — D6 named exactly two new siblings, and the ledger predates the mailbox roles that write to it, so gating it would "},{"id":"spn-58321","marks":["italic"],"text":"change"},{"id":"spn-58322","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58323","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1"},{"id":"spn-58324","text":" rather than preserve it."}]},{"id":"blk-37184","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58325","text":"Finding 5 — "},{"id":"spn-58326","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-58327","text":" bound mismatch — CONFIRMED; froze "},{"id":"spn-58328","marks":["code"],"text":"1 <= w <= 32"}]},{"id":"blk-37185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58329","text":"One constant, "},{"id":"spn-58330","marks":["code"],"text":"WC.MAILBOX_WIDTH_MAX"},{"id":"spn-58331","text":", read by both surfaces. The bug had real teeth: "},{"id":"spn-58332","marks":["code"],"text":"w = 33"},{"id":"spn-58333","text":" could seal and "},{"id":"spn-58334","marks":["bold"],"text":"earn a `SemanticArtifactID`"},{"id":"spn-58335","text":", then fail to lower to the oracle — an identity minted for a world that cannot run."}]},{"id":"blk-37186","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58336","text":"3. The three new rows"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-37188","spans":[{"id":"spn-58337","text":"Row"}]},{"id":"blk-37189","spans":[{"id":"spn-58338","text":"Proves"}]},{"id":"blk-37190","spans":[{"id":"spn-58339","text":"Assertions"}]}],"id":"blk-37187","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-37191","spans":[{"id":"spn-58340","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.16"}]},{"id":"blk-37192","spans":[{"id":"spn-58341","text":"the production seam: seal → view → "},{"id":"spn-58342","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-58343","text":"; D8 measured against the twin; tamper detection; two sends to one mailbox plus an equivocal send"}]},{"id":"blk-37193","spans":[{"id":"spn-58344","text":"10"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37194","spans":[{"id":"spn-58345","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.17"}]},{"id":"blk-37195","spans":[{"id":"spn-58346","text":"runtime schema exactness in both directions, including that stepping does not widen"}]},{"id":"blk-37196","spans":[{"id":"spn-58347","text":"8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37197","spans":[{"id":"spn-58348","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.18"}]},{"id":"blk-37198","spans":[{"id":"spn-58349","marks":["code"],"text":"w == 32"},{"id":"spn-58350","text":" seals, "},{"id":"spn-58351","marks":["code"],"text":"33"},{"id":"spn-58352","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-58353","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-58354","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-58355","marks":["code"],"text":"cap 0"},{"id":"spn-58356","text":" are typed rejects, oracle and IR agree"}]},{"id":"blk-37199","spans":[{"id":"spn-58357","text":"6"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-37200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58358","text":"Two of these I checked for teeth rather than trusting a green line:"}]},{"id":"blk-37201","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58359","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.16's tamper assertion"},{"id":"spn-58360","text":" is caught by the "},{"id":"spn-58361","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-58362","text":" check specifically — "},{"id":"spn-58363","marks":["code"],"text":"\"plan is not bound to its semantic artifact\""},{"id":"spn-58364","text":" — not by incidental structural validation. The declaration is genuinely inside the identity."}]}],"id":"blk-37202","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58365","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.17's \"stepping does not widen\""},{"id":"spn-58366","text":" fails when the old "},{"id":"spn-58367","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-58368","text":" behavior is restored, and passes otherwise."}]}],"id":"blk-37204","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-37206","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58369","text":"4. The reversal you should rule on"}]},{"id":"blk-37207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58370","marks":["bold"],"text":"Revision D said mailboxes do not belong in `CompilePlanV1`. Commit 8 puts them there. I want this ruled rather than assumed."}]},{"id":"blk-37208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58371","text":"My Revision D reasoning was that §10.12 proves "},{"id":"spn-58372","marks":["code"],"text":"_backend_content_hash"},{"id":"spn-58373","text":" is identical between a mailbox world and its twin, so the mailbox adds nothing physical and the backend-neutral plan should not carry it. That reasoning survives; the "},{"id":"spn-58374","marks":["bold"],"text":"conclusion"},{"id":"spn-58375","text":" does not, because it ignored that the plan is not only the lowering contract — it is also the object that is "},{"id":"spn-58376","marks":["italic"],"text":"sealed and bound to the artifact by reconstruction"},{"id":"spn-58377","text":". Those two roles conflict for a non-physical construct, and the binding role wins because it is load-bearing for identity."}]},{"id":"blk-37209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58378","text":"The alternative was to change how a plan binds to its artifact — carry canonical bytes instead of reconstructing. I rejected it: that is a larger change to a mechanism frozen at Phase 3D.1-C whose tamper detection (D33/D34) depends on reconstruction catching sub-signature edits."}]},{"id":"blk-37210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58379","text":"The shape I chose states D8 rather than assuming it:"}]},{"id":"blk-37211","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"plan[\"mailboxes\"] = [{\"id\", \"w\", \"cap\"}, …]      canonically sorted"},{"id":"blk-37212","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58380","text":"absent from "},{"id":"spn-58381","marks":["code"],"text":"object_order"},{"id":"spn-58382","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-58383","marks":["code"],"text":"object_index"},{"id":"spn-58384","text":" and from all three neutral signatures;"}]}],"id":"blk-37213","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58385","text":"may not collide with a physical object id;"}]}],"id":"blk-37215","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58386","text":"never read by "},{"id":"spn-58387","marks":["code"],"text":"compile_step_v6"},{"id":"spn-58388","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-37217","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-37219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58389","text":"§10.16 then "},{"id":"spn-58390","marks":["italic"],"text":"measures"},{"id":"spn-58391","text":" D8 instead of asserting it. Against the mailbox-free twin, the object index, all three neutral signatures, "},{"id":"spn-58392","marks":["code"],"text":"backend_layout_signature"},{"id":"spn-58393","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58394","marks":["code"],"text":"_backend_content_hash"},{"id":"spn-58395","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-58396","marks":["bold"],"text":"identical"},{"id":"spn-58397","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-58398","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-58399","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-58400","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"},{"id":"spn-58401","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58402","marks":["bold"],"text":"differ"},{"id":"spn-58403","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-37220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58404","text":"I now think this is strictly better than omission: an omitted declaration makes \"the mailbox contributes nothing physical\" "},{"id":"spn-58405","marks":["italic"],"text":"unfalsifiable"},{"id":"spn-58406","text":" at the plan layer, whereas a declaration the compiler demonstrably ignores makes it a measurement. But it is your call."}]},{"id":"blk-37221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58407","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cost:"},{"id":"spn-58408","text":" "},{"id":"spn-58409","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"},{"id":"spn-58410","text":" moves for "},{"id":"spn-58411","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-58412","text":" world, since the plan gained a field. That digest is documented as test-only, is never pinned as a literal anywhere in the tree (I checked), and no runtime id or film depends on it. No "},{"id":"spn-58413","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-58414","text":" and no "},{"id":"spn-58415","marks":["code"],"text":"BackendArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-58416","text":" of a mailbox-free world moved."}]},{"id":"blk-37222","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-58417","text":"5. A correction to my own Commit 7 memo"}]},{"id":"blk-37223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-58418","text":"I reported "},{"id":"spn-58419","marks":["bold"],"text":"two"},{"id":"spn-58420","text":" pre-existing failures. There are "},{"id":"spn-58421","marks":["bold"],"text":"three"},{"id":"spn-58422","text":". "},{"id":"spn-58423","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-58424","text":" was never in the sweep list I inherited, so I never ran it. It fails identically at "},{"id":"spn-58425","marks":["code"],"text":"HEAD"},{"id":"spn-58426","text":" with the Slice A changes stashed:"}]},{"id":"blk-37224","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[FAIL] L1) parse_wrl_core(format(graph)) == graph, 6 worlds\n[FAIL] L8) run inputs (claims) survive format -> parse"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-37226","spans":[{"id":"spn-58427","text":"Battery"}]},{"id":"blk-37227","spans":[{"id":"spn-58428","text":"Symptom"}]},{"id":"blk-37228","spans":[{"id":"spn-58429","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-37225","kind":"table","rows":